# Auto-generated lockfiles
/**/bun.lock
/**/package-lock.json
/**/pnpm-lock.yaml

# Build / test outputs
/**/dist/
/**/coverage/
/**/node_modules/
/**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Files Prettier has no parser for (no plugin loaded)
/**/.gitignore
/**/.nvmrc
/**/.npmrc
/**/.prettierignore
/**/*.toml

# VitePress dependency cache. `/**/dist/` above already covers
# `.vitepress/dist/`; nothing covered the cache. Until package.json moved here
# Prettier ran from the repo root and picked the rule up from the root
# .gitignore -- one of its two DEFAULT ignore paths, both resolved against the
# working directory rather than the config. From `docs/` there is no .gitignore
# to read, so 134 cache files became lint targets. eslint.config.js spells the
# same path out, for the same reason.
/**/.vitepress/cache/

# Markdown belongs to rumdl (.rumdl.toml, `mise run markdownlint`), which is the
# gate hk and CI actually run. The two formatters disagree and cannot both own a
# file: Prettier rewrites a loose list by putting a blank line between every
# item, which is precisely what rumdl's MD076 rejects -- running
# `prettier --write` over plan/IMPLEMENTATION.md turned a passing gate into a
# failing one. Prettier keeps .ts/.mts/.json/.vue/.css, where nothing competes
# with it.
/**/*.md

# Changeset internal cache
/**/.changeset/.cache/

# Rumdl cache
/**/.rumdl_cache/

# Local claude-mem scratch buffer -- gitignored, not project source.
# ESLint (`ignores`) and rumdl (`exclude`) already skip it.
/**/.remember/
